{"seq":12,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:56:50.491Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"bfcd86471efe89e61ed1c1d3cfc741106a07072c1fc0b5a4f1d55adf8dbfcbaa","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through all six of Moss's agent notes. Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated, dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025, dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday). Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire yard, Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the gate was clear.\n\nBefore these go in the deck:\n• Moss's 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal note both mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number.\n• #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central handoffs note belong to Pree's dealer account, not QFL. I left them out.\n• Marcus's own note from 14 Jul 2025 (not one of Moss's) also cites #4419, but there it's \"Gate 3 printer lag / BOL printout delay.\" That doesn't match Moss's scanner description, so check #4419 in the support system before you quote it.\n• Watch the spelling: \"Quarendon Freightways\" is a different company and not a customer. Nothing above is about them."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:56:56.373Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f063f5056ad85a89ffdca50078f880a52471785286035c8913ee5387c05f61ab","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I went through all six of Moss's notes and replied to Hollis in his DM. Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers turn up:\n\n1. **#4419**, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\". Barcode scanners at the gatehouse weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on the third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. **#PD-4492**, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Drivers on the 04:00 shift at the Eau Claire yard, Doors 14–18, weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and the customer confirmed the next morning that it was fixed.\n\nI also gave him these notes:\n- **Ticket #4419 descriptions don't match.** Marcus's own note from 14 Jul 2025 lists #4419 as a Gate 3 printer delay, not a scanner problem. Hollis should check that ticket in the support system before putting it in the deck.\n- **Two tickets left out.** Moss's Central handoffs note lists #4409 and #4412, but they're for Pree's dealer account, not Quarrendon.\n- **Two notes with no ticket numbers.** Two other Moss notes mention Quarrendon but give no ticket numbers.\n- **Name mix-up risk.** \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is a different company and not a customer. Nothing in the list is about them.\n\nEverything came from notes anyone can open, and ticket numbers aren't finance figures, so no approval was needed."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
